  message: "DONE in PR #2326 (dev 091922e7e). Both loops now read their futures in submission order, and that order is total: the registries sort by priority, then name. The same loop shape in ranking._compute_centrality_with_python is fixed too (its dict is written to sketch_precomputed.additional_file_centrality_scores).\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (2026-11-22, one tree, two runs per arm, PYTHONHASHSEED=0): mastodon sub-tree (app, db, lib, streaming): on dev 976cc8805 the two maps differ in 22 edge positions (the filed sighting, reproduced); with the fix they are the same sequence. pretix src/pretix: two fixed runs are the same sequence (two base runs were too, in these two runs). Unit tests: the first pass in registry order is made to finish last and the collected order is asserted; they were red on dev.\nTHE CANDIDATE FIX'S WARNING (it changes which holder wins in every remaining order-reading table; measure before landing): measured on nine trees, base vs fixed. Same node set and same edge multiset on eight (pretix, mastodon, ghostfolio, haskellers, flask-restful, cowboy, apollo-server, chatwoot). alertmanager: 2 edges retargeted (two Elm client calls now bind the Go API routes, before the React page routes of the same path): filed as its own item.\nNOT CHANGED: analysis_runs is still sorted by started_at at finalize (wall clock); the order of symbols inside one analyzer's result is that analyzer's. NOT MEASURED: more than two runs per arm; any tree other than these nine.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr1/RESULTS.md."  # e0cc
